    "**ADAM ID: **[sm\\_us6000qxae](https://api.adam.geospatial.wfp.org/api/collections/adam.adam_eq_events/items?uid=sm_us6000qxae) Magnitude 5.6 earthquake at 72.617 depth occurred on Aug 01 2025 100 km S of Vilyuchinsk, Russia. The epicentre of the earthquake was located at latitude 52.0305 longitude 158.3556. It impacted 476 people within 50km. WFP’s Automated Disaster Analysis and Mapping (ADAM) system is an operational system for collecting, analysing and mapping geospatial and socio-economic information following sudden onset humanitarian emergencies."
